From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:47:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm, KAPI: say why HDMI 3D frame packing is refused

Issue #33 (Khazar321, RTX 5090) and the reports of NTM-3D on an RTX 1080,
2080 SUPER, 4070 Ti SUPER and 5050 (LibreELEC forum, thread 30682, #172):
Kodi asks for a frame-packed mode of 1080p24 with the buffer that the frame
packing patch of nvidia-drm asks for (1920x2205 shown, LINEAR), and the test
commit is refused with EINVAL. Kodi then falls back to a 2D mode with the 3D
layout told by the vendor InfoFrame (top and bottom, then side by side half).
On the 2080 SUPER the commit that Kodi falls back to, the 2D mode with the
same new buffer, is refused too.

Every reason for that refusal in nvidia-drm was debug output
(NV_DRM_DEV_DEBUG_DRIVER, only with drm.debug), and some had none at all:
the framebuffer that has no NVKMS surface (its memory is not video memory,
nv_drm_framebuffer_init()), a rotated plane, an interlaced mode, a cursor, an
asynchronous flip, a right eye past 4 GiB, a framebuffer already used for
another geometry. What NVKMS said of a test of the mode set was debug output
of KAPI only.

Each of them now goes to the kernel log at info level, with what was given:
"Hades: HDMI 3D frame packing refused: ..." (the size and coordinates of the
plane, the flags and modifier of the framebuffer, the size, pitch and offset
of the eye that NVKMS did not register). The same reason is said once, then
again after 30 s, as a client retries a refused mode
(nv_drm_frame_packing_say()). KAPI says, for a mode set that puts a head in
HDMI 3D, a test one too, when NVKMS refused it, with its status and that of
each head (1 invalid mode, 2 invalid display, 6 invalid flip), and when the
request could not be made for NVKMS at all.

Nothing is decided differently: only what is logged. The reasons are what
the next report of #33 needs to fix the refusal itself.

Compiled with the compiler and flags of the build against Linux 7.3.5 with
the patches of the tree, every module of the open tree linked. Not run on a
GPU.
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c  | 43 ++++++++++++++----
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-fb.c    | 37 +++++++++++-----
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-utils.c | 22 +++++++++
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-utils.h | 16 +++++++
 src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi.c  | 54 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 154 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
index 4c5e96f..b64f4c7 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
@@ -1245,7 +1245,7 @@ plane_config_update_frame_packed(struct drm_plane *plane,
     int ret;
 
     if (plane->type != DRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY) {
-        NV_DRM_DEV_DEBUG_DRIVER(
+        NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(
             nv_dev,
             "Only the primary plane can be used in an HDMI 3D frame packed "
             "mode");
@@ -1260,16 +1260,22 @@ plane_config_update_frame_packed(struct drm_plane *plane,
         (plane_state->crtc_x != 0) || (plane_state->crtc_y != 0) ||
         (plane_state->crtc_w != mode->hdisplay) ||
         (plane_state->crtc_h != packed_height)) {
-        NV_DRM_DEV_DEBUG_DRIVER(
+        NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(
             nv_dev,
             "In an HDMI 3D frame packed mode the primary plane has to cover "
-            "%ux%u, unscaled",
-            mode->hdisplay, packed_height);
+            "%ux%u, unscaled (it is given source %ux%u+%u+%u, destination "
+            "%ux%u+%d+%d)",
+            mode->hdisplay, packed_height,
+            plane_state->src_w >> 16, plane_state->src_h >> 16,
+            plane_state->src_x >> 16, plane_state->src_y >> 16,
+            plane_state->crtc_w, plane_state->crtc_h,
+            plane_state->crtc_x, plane_state->crtc_y);
         return -EINVAL;
     }
 
     if ((plane->rotation_property != NULL) &&
         (plane_state->rotation != DRM_MODE_ROTATE_0)) {
+        NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(nv_dev, "the primary plane is rotated or reflected");
         return -EINVAL;
     }
 
@@ -1313,6 +1319,21 @@ plane_req_config_update(struct drm_plane *plane,
 
     req_config->config.surface = to_nv_framebuffer(plane_state->fb)->pSurface;
     if (req_config->config.surface == NULL) {
+        /*
+         * Hades: a framebuffer whose memory is not video memory has no NVKMS
+         * surface (nv_drm_framebuffer_init()): said where it refuses a frame
+         * packed commit (issue #33)
+         */
+        if (nv_drm_mode_is_frame_packed(&crtc_state->mode)) {
+            NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(nv_dev,
+                              "the framebuffer (%ux%u, format %p4cc, modifier "
+                              "0x%llx) has no NVKMS surface: its memory is not "
+                              "video memory, which the display engine does "
+                              "not scan out",
+                              plane_state->fb->width, plane_state->fb->height,
+                              &plane_state->fb->format->format,
+                              (unsigned long long)plane_state->fb->modifier);
+        }
         return -EINVAL;
     }
 
@@ -1815,6 +1836,8 @@ static int __nv_drm_cursor_atomic_check(struct drm_plane *plane,
              */
             if ((plane_state->fb != NULL) &&
                 nv_drm_mode_is_frame_packed(&crtc_state->mode)) {
+                NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(to_nv_device(plane->dev),
+                                  "a cursor is set on the head");
                 return -EINVAL;
             }
 
@@ -1888,6 +1911,8 @@ static int nv_drm_plane_atomic_check(struct drm_plane *plane,
              */
             if (nv_drm_mode_is_frame_packed(&crtc_state->mode) &&
                 __is_async_flip_requested(plane, crtc_state)) {
+                NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(to_nv_device(plane->dev),
+                                  "an asynchronous flip is asked for");
                 return -EINVAL;
             }
 
@@ -2855,6 +2880,7 @@ static int nv_drm_crtc_atomic_check_frame_packed(
     /* The display hardware packs progressive frames only */
     if ((crtc_state->mode.flags &
          (DRM_MODE_FLAG_INTERLACE | DRM_MODE_FLAG_DBLSCAN)) != 0) {
+        NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(nv_dev, "the mode is interlaced or doublescan");
         return -EINVAL;
     }
 
@@ -2871,7 +2897,7 @@ static int nv_drm_crtc_atomic_check_frame_packed(
                 nv_connector->type == NVKMS_CONNECTOR_TYPE_HDMI,
                 nv_connector->dual_mode_tmds,
                 nv_connector->frame_packing_advertised)) {
-            NV_DRM_DEV_DEBUG_DRIVER(
+            NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(
                 nv_dev,
                 "The display does not advertise HDMI 3D frame packing");
             return -EINVAL;
@@ -2882,10 +2908,11 @@ static int nv_drm_crtc_atomic_check_frame_packed(
             /* Hades: nor HDR10PLUS_VSIF */
             (to_nv_drm_connector_state(connector_state)->hdr10plus_vsif !=
              NULL)) {
-            NV_DRM_DEV_DEBUG_DRIVER(
+            NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(
                 nv_dev,
-                "NV_HDMI_VSIF_METADATA cannot be set in an HDMI 3D frame "
-                "packed mode");
+                "NV_HDMI_VSIF_METADATA or HDR10PLUS_VSIF is set on the "
+                "connector, whose vendor InfoFrame would take the place of the "
+                "one that tells the display of frame packing");
             return -EINVAL;
         }
     }
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-fb.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-fb.c
index 4b372eb..cfdd828 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-fb.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-fb.c
@@ -393,22 +393,28 @@ int nv_drm_framebuffer_get_frame_packed_surfaces(
 
     if ((nv_fb->pSurface == NULL) ||
         (nv_gem == NULL) || (nv_gem->pMemory == NULL)) {
+        NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(nv_dev,
+                          "the framebuffer (%ux%u) has no NVKMS surface or no "
+                          "memory of NVKMS: it cannot be scanned out (not video "
+                          "memory, or not memory that NVKMS imported)",
+                          fb->width, fb->height);
         return -EINVAL;
     }
 
     if (((fb->flags & DRM_MODE_FB_MODIFIERS) == 0) ||
         (fb->modifier != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR)) {
-        NV_DRM_DEV_DEBUG_DRIVER(
+        NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(
             nv_dev,
-            "HDMI 3D frame packing needs a framebuffer created with "
-            "DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR");
+            "it needs a framebuffer created with DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR "
+            "(this one: flags 0x%x, modifier 0x%llx)",
+            fb->flags, (unsigned long long)fb->modifier);
         return -EINVAL;
     }
 
     if ((fb->format->num_planes != 1) ||
         nv_drm_format_is_yuv(fb->format->format) ||
         !nv_drm_format_to_nvkms_format(fb->format->format, &format)) {
-        NV_DRM_DEV_DEBUG_DRIVER(
+        NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(
             nv_dev,
             "HDMI 3D frame packing needs a single plane RGB framebuffer");
         return -EINVAL;
@@ -419,7 +425,7 @@ int nv_drm_framebuffer_get_frame_packed_surfaces(
     if ((eye_height == 0) ||
         (right_eye_row < eye_height) ||
         (((uint64_t)right_eye_row + eye_height) > fb->height)) {
-        NV_DRM_DEV_DEBUG_DRIVER(
+        NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(
             nv_dev,
             "Framebuffer of %u lines is too small for two eyes of %u lines, "
             "the second one from line %u",
@@ -431,6 +437,8 @@ int nv_drm_framebuffer_get_frame_packed_surfaces(
         (uint64_t)fb->offsets[0] + ((uint64_t)fb->pitches[0] * right_eye_row);
 
     if (right_eye_offset > U32_MAX) {
+        NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(nv_dev, "the right eye begins past 4 GiB (byte %llu)",
+                          right_eye_offset);
         return -EINVAL;
     }
 
@@ -444,6 +452,13 @@ int nv_drm_framebuffer_get_frame_packed_surfaces(
         if ((nv_fb->frame_packed.eye_height == eye_height) &&
             (nv_fb->frame_packed.right_eye_row == right_eye_row)) {
             ret = 0;
+        } else {
+            NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(nv_dev,
+                              "the framebuffer was used in a frame packed mode "
+                              "of eyes of %u lines from line %u, not %u from %u",
+                              nv_fb->frame_packed.eye_height,
+                              nv_fb->frame_packed.right_eye_row,
+                              eye_height, right_eye_row);
         }
         goto done;
     }
@@ -460,9 +475,11 @@ int nv_drm_framebuffer_get_frame_packed_surfaces(
     pLeftSurface = nvKms->createSurface(nv_dev->pDevice, &params);
 
     if (pLeftSurface == NULL) {
-        NV_DRM_DEV_DEBUG_DRIVER(
+        NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(
             nv_dev,
-            "Failed to create the left eye NvKmsKapiSurface");
+            "NVKMS did not register the left eye as a surface (%ux%u, pitch "
+            "%u, at byte %u)",
+            fb->width, eye_height, fb->pitches[0], fb->offsets[0]);
         goto done;
     }
 
@@ -476,11 +493,11 @@ int nv_drm_framebuffer_get_frame_packed_surfaces(
          * that is aligned as its display hardware needs, and the right eye
          * starts pitch * right_eye_row bytes into the framebuffer.
          */
-        NV_DRM_DEV_DEBUG_DRIVER(
+        NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(
             nv_dev,
-            "Failed to create the right eye NvKmsKapiSurface at offset %llu "
+            "NVKMS did not register the right eye as a surface at byte %llu "
             "(line %u, pitch %u): the offset may not be aligned as NVKMS "
-            "requires",
+            "requires (1024 bytes)",
             right_eye_offset, right_eye_row, fb->pitches[0]);
         nvKms->destroySurface(nv_dev->pDevice, pLeftSurface);
         goto done;
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-utils.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-utils.c
index 87e2222..ef7ebca 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-utils.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-utils.c
@@ -20,6 +20,9 @@
  * DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
  */
 
+#include <linux/jiffies.h>
+#include <linux/spinlock.h>
+
 #include "nvidia-drm-conftest.h" /* NV_DRM_AVAILABLE */
 
 #if defined(NV_DRM_AVAILABLE)
@@ -243,6 +246,25 @@ void drm_mode_to_nvkms_display_mode(const struct drm_display_mode *src,
  * only layout NVKMS can drive; a mode with any other layout is treated as its
  * 2D mode.
  */
+bool nv_drm_frame_packing_say(const char *why)
+{
+    static DEFINE_SPINLOCK(lock);
+    static const char *last;
+    static unsigned long last_at;
+    unsigned long flags;
+    bool say;
+
+    spin_lock_irqsave(&lock, flags);
+    say = (why != last) || time_after(jiffies, last_at + 30 * HZ);
+    if (say) {
+        last = why;
+        last_at = jiffies;
+    }
+    spin_unlock_irqrestore(&lock, flags);
+
+    return say;
+}
+
 bool nv_drm_mode_is_frame_packed(const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
 {
     return (mode->flags & DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_MASK) ==
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-utils.h b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-utils.h
index a5fdce2..0beac46 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-utils.h
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-utils.h
@@ -51,6 +51,22 @@ void drm_mode_to_nvkms_display_mode(const struct drm_display_mode *src,
 
 bool nv_drm_mode_is_frame_packed(const struct drm_display_mode *mode);
 
+/*
+ * Hades: why an HDMI 3D frame packed commit is refused, in the kernel log at info level (issue
+ * #33: the reasons were debug output, which no report has). Each reason once, then again after
+ * 30 s, as a client retries a refused mode (nv_drm_frame_packing_say()).
+ */
+bool nv_drm_frame_packing_say(const char *why);
+
+#define NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(__dev, __fmt, ...)                                  \
+    do {                                                                      \
+        if (nv_drm_frame_packing_say(__fmt)) {                                \
+            NV_DRM_DEV_LOG_INFO(__dev,                                        \
+                                "Hades: HDMI 3D frame packing refused: "      \
+                                __fmt, ##__VA_ARGS__);                        \
+        }                                                                     \
+    } while (0)
+
 #endif /* NV_DRM_AVAILABLE */
 
 #endif /* __NVIDIA_DRM_UTILS_H__ */
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi.c
index 07dcc18..fee9934 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi.c
@@ -3738,6 +3738,25 @@ static NvBool NvKmsKapiRequestedModeSetConfigToKms(
 }
 
 
+/*
+ * Hades: the request sets a head in an HDMI 3D frame packed mode (issue #33: what NVKMS said of such
+ * a mode set was debug output only)
+ */
+static NvBool HadesRequestHasHdmi3D(
+    const struct NvKmsKapiRequestedModeSetConfig *requestedConfig)
+{
+    NvU32 head;
+
+    for (head = 0; head < ARRAY_LEN(requestedConfig->headRequestedConfig); head++) {
+        if ((requestedConfig->headsMask & (1 << head)) &&
+            requestedConfig->headRequestedConfig[head].modeSetConfig.bActive &&
+            requestedConfig->headRequestedConfig[head].modeSetConfig.mode.timings.flags.hdmi3D) {
+            return NV_TRUE;
+        }
+    }
+    return NV_FALSE;
+}
+
 static NvBool KmsSetMode(
     struct NvKmsKapiDevice *device,
     const struct NvKmsKapiRequestedModeSetConfig *requestedConfig,
@@ -3757,6 +3776,14 @@ static NvBool KmsSetMode(
                                               requestedConfig,
                                               params,
                                               commit)) {
+        /* Hades: issue #33 */
+        if (HadesRequestHasHdmi3D(requestedConfig)) {
+            nvEvoLog(EVO_LOG_INFO,
+                     "Hades: [kapi][GPU Id 0x%08x] HDMI 3D frame packing: the mode set "
+                     "could not be made into a request of NVKMS (a layer, the output "
+                     "transfer function or the LUT of a head was refused first)",
+                     device->gpuId);
+        }
         goto done;
     }
 
@@ -3792,6 +3819,33 @@ static NvBool KmsSetMode(
     {
         int i;
 
+        /*
+         * Hades: a mode set with HDMI 3D frame packing that NVKMS refused, a test
+         * one too, with its statuses (issue #33)
+         */
+        if (HadesRequestHasHdmi3D(requestedConfig)) {
+            char heads[96];
+            int n = 0;
+
+            heads[0] = '\0';
+            for (i = 0; (i < ARRAY_LEN(params->reply.disp[0].head)) &&
+                        (n < (int)sizeof(heads) - 16); i++) {
+                if (params->reply.disp[0].head[i].status != 0) {
+                    n += nvkms_snprintf(heads + n, sizeof(heads) - n, " head %d: %d",
+                                        i, params->reply.disp[0].head[i].status);
+                }
+            }
+            nvEvoLog(EVO_LOG_INFO,
+                     "Hades: [kapi][GPU Id 0x%08x] HDMI 3D frame packing: %s mode set "
+                     "refused by NVKMS: status %d, disp 0 status %d,%s (enum "
+                     "NvKmsSetModeStatus, NvKmsSetModeOneDispStatus and "
+                     "NvKmsSetModeOneHeadStatus of nvkms-api.h; a head: 1 invalid mode, "
+                     "2 invalid display, 6 invalid flip)",
+                     device->gpuId, commit ? "a" : "a test of a",
+                     params->reply.status, params->reply.disp[0].status,
+                     heads[0] ? heads : " no head with a status");
+        }
+
         nvKmsKapiLogDeviceDebug(
             device,
             "NVKMS_IOCTL_SET_MODE failed!  Status:\n");
